INCIDENT FIRST (duplicate server):
(a) app/server.mjs: the inbox scanner and the auto-montage pump (setInterval(scanInbox) + first scan/pumpAuto) moved into demarrerTaches(), called only in the server.listen callback. New server.on('error'): if the server is not yet listening (EADDRINUSE or any listen error), it writes the reason to runtime/cache/erreurs-serveur.log ("demarrage refuse : port … indisponible") and stderr, then calls process.exit(98) (SORTIE_PORT_PRIS). After startup, errors are only logged. A duplicate now dies in 0.14 s without touching _revision.json.
(b) editeur.ps1 rewritten (LF and ASCII messages kept). Startup order:
- writes the lock runtime\cache\lanceur-<port>.json (pid + StartTime in UTC ticks);
- stops OTHER, OLDER launcher loops BEFORE touching the server. A launcher is a powershell.exe/pwsh.exe process, not itself and not an ancestor, whose command line contains this script's full path. The parent of the current server also counts if its command line contains "editeur.ps1" or has no -Command;
- then, re-reading each pass, stops the process listening on the port plus every "node <this folder>\app\server.mjs" (even one without a port, i.e. an old zombie duplicate), and waits until the port is free (10 s max, otherwise exit 2);
- in the loop: never respawns after exit code 98 (message, exit 2). Exits cleanly if a newer launcher took the lock (newest wins: two quick double-clicks never kill each other). Restarts after 2 s on a crash (15 s after 3 quick crashes). ExitCode is read reliably ($srv.Handle).
- EDITEUR_PORT / EDITEUR_SANS_NAVIGATEUR=1 allow tests on a copy.
"Editeur Sami.cmd" is unchanged.

QUALITY CONTROLLER (part of the wiring came from the interrupted attempt; I reviewed and kept it, and completed or fixed the rest):
(1) CLI `python -m editeur controle <projet|reel.json|job.json> [--reel] [--video --debut] [--sortie] [--enregistrer]` prints one JSON line (report + resume). Routes:
- POST /api/reels/:p/:v/controle {} runs the montage pass (job; the resume goes into reel.controle and onto the Révision card);
- POST …/controle {video, format?, debut?} runs the video pass (job, one at a time; uses the reel of that exact export (export.json) or the job.json next to a preview);
- GET …/controle returns {montage, exports[], dernier, resume}.
auto._finish now also writes the full report to runtime/cache/controle/<projet>-script/montage (new helpers controle.dossier_rapport / ecrire_rapport). The card note comes through info['controle'].
(2) Révision UI (revision.tsx + /* controle */ CSS):
- the player and the "Contrôle qualité" panel now sit side by side. Before, the panel squeezed the player down to a thumbnail, as seen in my first capture;
- the panel shows a score /10 with colour, the verdict, and Montage / Export tabs;
- each problem shows its severity badge, a clickable ▶ 0:26,0 time that pauses, seeks and draws a blinking red frame at its zone, and a → suggestion;
- buttons: « Relancer le contrôle » and « 🔎 Contrôler l'export » on every finished export;
- the score is on the list card, and « Je la prends » asks for confirmation when there is a blocking problem.
(3) After every successful export in the queue, controleApresExport runs the video pass in the background (the queue does not wait). The result goes into job.controle and onto the matching Révision export (e.controle / controleEtat). EDITEUR_CONTROLE_EXPORT=0 disables it.
(4) Plugin: the tools controle (modes dernier/montage/export), refaire_passage, choregraphie and banque_catalogue (read-only) were present from the first attempt; I reviewed them and tested them over stdio. No delete tool. The editeur-sami skill text gained a section on the launcher and port 98, plus an "outdated score" tip; the other skills were already up to date.
(5) controle.py synced with the renderer as it stood at 03:07:
- the Node bridge now also returns, per frame, studioView (studio camera) and cutoutFallbackMix (cutout fallback). It also returns scene sizes from studioCardSize, chiffre positions from studioGraphicSpot, studioGrade per shot, and what the renderer supports;
- _hud: no more « VIDÉO 1 » title or clock; only the brand name when the brand has no logo, hidden during a fallback;
- _carte_studio: glass cards with the real StudioCard text sizes; the cards have a bright border, so they are never estimated as "terne";
- chiffre: StudioMetric at the studioGraphicSpot position;
- _sous_titres (studio): signsEm character widths, shrink to 80 %, balanced lines; captions are hidden only while a chiffre or giant word is on screen (saysWords);
- visibles: the V2 userGraphic rule;
- face, backgrounds (Fonds), tiers-vide and the cutout audit use the camera rectangle (ctx.rect);
- cadre-fige: camera moves of ≥ 2.5 % in 1.5 s count as relances; zoom-invisible only if the renderer has no camera;
- the RVM fallback field is now in the cutout check: detourage-repli becomes a "conseil" (the renderer shows the original take), with its ranges; video-pass frames inside a fallback range are skipped;
- integration-lumiere is measured after studioGrade;
- a 4 px tolerance at the 6 % safe zone;
- NEW: a video older than remotion/src gets the "rendu-ancien" conseil. For such a video, the per-element image checks are skipped and the cutout audit uses the rectangle without camera.

